    "title": "From Memorial High physics class to NASA Moon mission, McAllen engineer makes history - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jose De Leon III ,\n11 hours ago A McAllen Memorial High School graduate is helping lead NASA's first crewed mission to the Moon in more than 50 years. Debbie Whitis Korth graduated from Memorial in 1987 and is one of the chief engineers behind Artemis II. Korth now serves as Orion Deputy Program Manager at NASA and... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
